  "question": {
    "text": "If the radius of first orbit of $\\mathrm{H}$ atom is $a_0$, the deBroglie wavelength of an electron in the third orbit is",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "9Hx6T",
      "text": "\n$4 \\pi a_0$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "1KbF4",
      "text": "\n$8 \\pi a_0$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "z7wDe",
      "text": "\n$6 \\pi a_0$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    },
    {
      "id": "eISU4",
      "text": "\n$2 \\pi a_0$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "$r_n=a_0 n^2$\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n& r=a_0 \\times(3)^2=9 a_0 \\\\\n& m v r=\\frac{n h}{2 \\pi} \\\\\n& m v=\\frac{n h}{2 \\pi \\mathrm{r}}=\\frac{3 h}{2 \\pi \\times 9 a_0}=\\frac{h}{6 \\pi a_0} \\\\\n& \\lambda=\\frac{h}{m v}=\\frac{h}{h} \\times 6 \\pi a_0=6 \\pi a_0\n\\end{aligned}\n$$",
    "image": null
